# Root-level .dockerignore — applies to every service whose docker-compose
# build context is the repo root: intake-service and eligibility-service
# (adr/0005-eligibility-agent-runtime-and-resilience.md), records-service
# (Stage 3 — imports libs.patient_view_agent), gateway (it must copy
# config/roles.yaml, the live RBAC permission source, which lives outside its
# own directory), and now scheduling-service, interop-service, and
# roi-service (OBS-M02, Stage 7 smoke-test discovery: all three import
# libs/ — libs.safe_logging, and scheduling/roi's Stage 6 libs.metrics —
# which a per-service build context could never see; the image built fine
# but the container crashed at startup with ModuleNotFoundError, invisible
# to CI and to pytest, which imports directly from the repo checkout).
#
# Every root-context service now needs every other service's directory
# present in the context (none is excluded below) — that costs a few KB of
# context and nothing else, since each Dockerfile only COPYs the paths it
# names.
.git/
.github/
frontend/
node_modules/
# W10 Final 2 Stage 2: `docs/*` (not a bare `docs/`) excludes only docs/'s
# DIRECT children, so docs/RagDocs — the approved synthetic policy corpus's
# actual source content records-service's Dockerfile now COPYs for
# db/policy_corpus_prepare.py — can be individually re-included below
# without bringing back the rest of docs/ (planning/handover/analysis/
# client-inputs, none of which any service build needs). A bare `!docs/`
# re-inclusion was tried and rejected: it un-ignores the whole docs/ tree,
# not just RagDocs, since nothing else re-excludes those other
# subdirectories once the parent itself is un-ignored.
docs/*
!docs/RagDocs
!docs/RagDocs/**
# W10 Metrics Stage 5: db/policy_corpus_evaluate.py (re-included below) reads
# these two fixed, synthetic evaluation-case/citation-alias files — same
# per-ancestor-level re-inclusion requirement as docs/RagDocs above (a bare
# `!docs/client-inputs/2026-08-24/evaluations` alone does not reach through
# `docs/*`'s exclusion of its own direct-child ancestor,
# docs/client-inputs). No other client-inputs content (fixtures/, other
# dated directories) is re-included.
!docs/client-inputs
!docs/client-inputs/2026-08-24
!docs/client-inputs/2026-08-24/evaluations
!docs/client-inputs/2026-08-24/evaluations/**
adr/
tests/
.claude/
.codex_tmp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# db/ is mounted into the Postgres container at runtime (docker-compose.yml);
# it is not part of any Python service's build.
#
# w8-planner-2 P2 (adr/0012), review round 1 fix (B1): TWO exceptions —
# intake-service's Dockerfile COPYs the ssn/dob/notes backfill script
# (db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_existing_phi.py), and records-service's
# Dockerfile COPYs the agent-draft-text backfill script (adr/0012
# follow-up, db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_agent_draft_text.py) — so
# `make up`/`make seed`/`make phi-backfill` can run both via `docker
# compose exec`. The negation is listed at every parent level for each; a
# bare `!db/migrations/scripts/<file>` alone does not re-include a file
# whose ancestor directory was already excluded.
db/
!db/migrations/
!db/migrations/scripts/
!db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_existing_phi.py
!db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_agent_draft_text.py
# W10 Final 2 Stage 2: same reasoning — records-service's Dockerfile COPYs
# this single idempotent RAG-preparation wrapper so `make rag-prepare` can
# run it via `docker compose exec`, without needing the sibling CLI scripts
# (policy_corpus_ingest.py/policy_corpus_evaluate.py) it does not import.
!db/policy_corpus_prepare.py
# W10 Metrics Stage 5: records-service's Dockerfile now also COPYs
# policy_corpus_evaluate.py so `make rag-eval-publish` can run its
# --publish flag via `docker compose exec`.
!db/policy_corpus_evaluate.py
# W10 Metrics Stage 5 completion-gate fix: `make rag-eval-publish`'s
# patient-record-corpus half (libs/rag_eval/harness.py, via libs/rag_corpus
# and libs/rag_eval's own identity/clinical-field lookups) reads these three
# fixed, synthetic seed fixtures directly off disk — this was never
# exercised inside a container before, only on a host checkout, so the gap
# went unnoticed until a real run. Same deterministic generator inputs
# db/seed/generate_seed.py already produces seed.sql from; never real
# patient data.
!db/seed/
!db/seed/patients.csv
!db/seed/encounters.csv
!db/seed/goldset.json
